{%- comment -%}
  Theme-level robots.txt.

  Shopify serves a sensible default robots.txt (it already disallows /search, /cart,
  /checkout, /account and the ?sort_by / ?filter parameter URLs), and this template
  preserves every one of those rules verbatim via robots.default_groups. It exists so
  crawl rules are an explicit, version-controlled part of the theme instead of an
  invisible platform default — if we ever need to open or close a path to crawlers,
  it is a reviewable diff here rather than a setting nobody can see.

  The only additions on top of the defaults are a handful of low-value commercial
  crawlers that spend crawl bandwidth without ever sending a customer. Search engines
  that actually drive leads (Googlebot, Bingbot, DuckDuckBot, Applebot) and the
  Google Business Profile crawler are untouched.

  Do not add "Disallow: /" here under any circumstances — it would deindex the site.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent }}

  {% for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{ rule }}
  {% endfor -%}

  {%- if group.sitemap -%}
    {{ group.sitemap }}
  {%- endif -%}
{% endfor %}

# --- Kilowash additions (BouldHQ) ---
# Commercial crawlers that consume bandwidth without sending traffic.
User-agent: MJ12bot
Disallow: /

User-agent: DotBot
Disallow: /

User-agent: PetalBot
Disallow: /

# Explicit sitemap declaration so it is discoverable even if a future default changes.
Sitemap: {{ request.origin }}/sitemap.xml
